Subject: [PATCH] keepalived-sync: do not restart/stop dnsmasq on state change

The 551-dnsmasq hotplug script stops dnsmasq when the node becomes BACKUP
(set_stop_if_backup) and restarts it on MASTER (set_restart_if_master).

On OpenWrt dnsmasq also provides DNS, and the router's own resolv.conf points
at it, so stopping it on a BACKUP node breaks name resolution for the node
itself and for any client that uses that node as an alternate main router.

Drop both actions so that 551-dnsmasq no longer touches the service on
NOTIFY_MASTER/NOTIFY_BACKUP. The add_sync_file entries are kept, so the
dhcp config and lease file stay on the sync whitelist. Whether DHCP is
served on a given node is left to the user's own keepalived hooks.

---
diff --git a/net/keepalived/files/etc/hotplug.d/keepalived/551-dnsmasq b/net/keepalived/files/etc/hotplug.d/keepalived/551-dnsmasq
index 8254521..4e41354 100644
--- a/net/keepalived/files/etc/hotplug.d/keepalived/551-dnsmasq
+++ b/net/keepalived/files/etc/hotplug.d/keepalived/551-dnsmasq
@@ -5,9 +5,6 @@
 
 set_service_name dnsmasq
 
-set_restart_if_master
-set_stop_if_backup
-
 add_sync_file /etc/config/dhcp
 add_sync_file /tmp/dhcp.leases
